            <ArticleTitle>Fixed drug eruption to rofecoxib.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rofecoxib, used for dysmenorrhea, caused a herpetiform fixed drug eruption predominantly involving the lips with classic clinical and histological findings in a red-brown lesion on the dorsal hand.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
